  "layout": "verse",
  "note": "Thackeray's 10-stanza selection of Prudentius, Peristephanon III (St. Eulalia), from Translations from Prudentius (London: George Bell and Sons, 1890), printed pages 120-125 (IA leaves 202-207), with Latin and English on facing pages. It is not the whole poem: a row of asterisks on pp. 122 and 123 marks the stanzas he left out. The Internet Archive identifier translationsfro00thacgoog is mislabeled in the catalog as Hilario Cuevas, Estudio práctico sobre el cultivo del café (Mexico, 1895). The files are the Harvard University Google Books scan of Thackeray 1890 (Google Books id 0zBRe61LLy0C), confirmed from the printed title page ('Translations from Prudentius ... Francis St. John Thackeray ... London: George Bell and Sons ... 1890') and from the PDF title. The catalog date and publisher are not used. English and Latin are both hosted, in the order of the scan, with verse line and stanza breaks kept as printed."
